# DreamAI Claude Code Build Playbook: {{PRODUCT_NAME}} (the product)

The DreamAI recipe for building a spec-driven product with Claude Code — spec-driven development, test-driven
development, contracts-first, library-grounded coding — on top of the **RAG_Wright engine** (open-core). The
product depends on the engine one-way (Product → Engine) and hand-builds its own orchestration (GraphWright, the
orchestration compiler, is PARKED per engine ADR-0052).

> **FILL THESE FIRST** (then delete this block): `{{PRODUCT_NAME}}`, `{{PRODUCT_DOMAIN}}`, `{{ENGINE_PATH}}`,
> `{{ENGINE_DEP}}`, `{{ENGINE_FLOOR}}`, `{{STACK}}`, the `{{SPEC}}`/`{{PLAN}}`/`{{TASKS}}` + `{{REQ_SCHEME}}`/`{{AC_SCHEME}}` scheme,
> the grounding-lane paths, and `{{PROJECT_FRONTEND_SKILL}}`. The boundary, skills, phases, per-task loop,
> grounding discipline, and memory/commit rules stay as written. Companion to this repo's `CLAUDE.md`.

> Conventions: acronyms expanded on first use, no em dashes, plain phrasing.

