## 3. CLAUDE.md standing rules (load-bearing summary)

```
- {{SPEC}} is the single source of truth. Do not invent requirements; if unspecified, ask.
- Product -> Engine, one way. Never modify the engine from this repo. Consume it only through
  rag_wright.api; never access the store (ArcadeDB) directly.
- INDEX BEFORE CODE. No code calling a library is written before it is in a graph. Declaring/
  installing is not calling: declare+install -> refresh graph -> write the grounded call.
- Ground engine API calls against the `engine` lane (the installed rag_wright package); ground
  your own libs against `project`.
- The reference pack (contract/compliance) is the engine's EXAMPLE, not your domain — author your
  own .ttl pack + capabilities.
- Self-hosted model: deploy it with adeploy_model_server (the locked qwen-vllm-modal setup) and put
  server.model_id in EngineConfig.models; never hand-edit VLLM_BASE_URL for it.
- Workspaces: one corpus + one EngineConfig + one cache_dir per tenant; register capabilities once
  per process; the engine's docs/workspaces.md says what is per workspace, per call, per process.
- Per task: ground, define the contract, failing test (TDD), implement to green, verify, short ADR
  if an architectural decision was made, update docs. A LIVE engine-seam test on every integration.
- One task at a time; stop for approval; commit each approved task atomically from a clean tree.
- Python: uv only (uv run / uv add), never bare python/pip.
```

